  "index.heroTitle": "SMART TRANSFORMATION IN EDUCATION WITH ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE",
  "index.heroSubtitle": "Empowering Education with AI – Erasmus+ Small-Scale Partnership KA210-SCH-DA028F59",
  "index.aboutHeading": "About the Project",
  "index.projectAcronym": "Project Acronym:",
  "index.projectDesc1": "The project \"SMART TRANSFORMATION IN EDUCATION WITH ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE\" (Smart edu AI) is a Small-scale partnership in school education (KA210-SCH) under the Erasmus+ Programme. It has a duration of 24 months, starting on January 1, 2025, and ending on December 31, 2026, with a total lump sum budget of €60,000",
  "index.objectivesHeading": "Main Objectives and Priorities: The project aims to integrate Artificial Intelligence (AI) technologies into educational processes to support individual learning and development. Its core objectives are: • Using Student-Centered AI Applications in the Learning Process: Offering personalized learning experiences tailored to individual styles and paces through adaptive learning technologies. • AI Training for Teachers: Enhancing teachers' digital skills to enable them to create more personalized and effective learning environments. • Individual Learning Analysis and Feedback Mechanism: Utilizing AI to analyze student learning data, identify strengths and weaknesses, and adapt teaching strategies accordingly. • Ensuring Equality of Opportunity in Education: Employing AI technologies to create an equitable learning environment for disadvantaged students, helping overcome barriers like language differences and special needs",
  "common.participatingOrgs": "Participating Organizations",
  "index.partner_eurolab": "Eurolab for Teachers was founded five years ago by experienced teachers and trainers, with a mission to deliver high-quality professional development across Europe. Through the Erasmus+ program, a range of specialised courses blends modern teaching strategies, innovative tools, and intercultural perspectives—enhancing skills, fostering creativity, and promoting both personal and professional growth.",
  "index.partner_krakow": "Founded in 1627 by Blessed Mother Zofia Maciejowska-Czeska, is Poland’s oldest girls’ school, now coeducational for ages 7–19. Grounded in Christian values and nearly 400 years of tradition, it blends heritage with modern teaching. The school offers diverse extracurriculars like music, sports, language exchanges and international partnerships.",
  "index.partner_duzce": "Public institution for gifted students, specializing in innovative research, teacher training, and AI project testing. Provides collaborative support and education for gifted students in an inclusive environment. The center carries out numerous national and international project activities, including intelligence game tournaments, digital design workshops, eTwinning projects, and math olympiads.",
  "common.website": "Website",
  "index.partner_france": "NGO supporting disadvantaged groups through educational, cultural, and digital projects, with expertise in AI and ethics. Offers training on technology planning models, technology integration strategies, and digital tools such as Web 2.0, augmented and virtual reality, and generative AI. France Culture Connection was selected for its outstanding work in AI education and its proven track record in developing advanced educational materials.",
  "index_centro-pblico-integrado-o-cruce-spain": "Centro Público Integrado O Cruce (Spain)",
  "index.partner_spain": "Multilingual public center recognized for innovative teaching, focusing on disadvantaged students and AI impact analysis.A public integrated multilingual center (kindergarten, primary, and secondary) with about 400 students. It is recognized as one of the most innovative schools and is part of the Galician digital education network. It participates in multiple educational innovation projects.",
  "index_erasmus": "Erasmus +",
  "index.smart_edu_desc1": "The project titled \"SMART TRANSFORMATION IN EDUCATION WITH ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE\" (Smart edu AI) will run for 24 months from January 1, 2025, to December 31, 2026. Its main goal is to support personalized learning and development by integrating artificial intelligence (AI) technologies into education. The project focuses on developing student-centered AI applications, training teachers in AI tools, and ensuring equal educational opportunities. It also emphasizes individual learning analysis, data analytics, and sustainable environment skills.",
  "index.smart_edu_desc2": "Aligned with Erasmus+ priorities, the project addresses digital transformation, environmental sustainability, climate action, and teacher support. Key themes include AI and data use, ecological skills, inclusion, equality, and non-discrimination.Target groups include students across primary, secondary, and high school levels, especially disadvantaged learners, students with special needs, language barriers, and gifted students. Teachers, educational institutions, administrators, and policymakers are also involved.",
  "index.smart_edu_desc3": "Key activities involve AI-assisted training and workshops for teachers and students, carbon footprint reduction and sustainability workshops, AI applications in digital design and music practice, AI-supported teaching for disadvantaged students, augmented reality and simulation science experiments, and feedback sessions. Four main activities are led by partners in France, Spain, Turkey, and Poland.",
  "index.smart_edu_desc4": "Expected outcomes include enhanced student learning experiences and academic performance, improved digital literacy for teachers, a data repository, innovative teaching methods, and increased environmental awareness. AI integration will personalize education, improve efficiency, and reduce teachers' workload.",
  "index.smart_edu_desc5": "The coordinating organization is Eurolab for Teachers (Poland), with partner organizations France Culture Connection (France), Düzce Milli Egemenlik Bilim ve&nbsp;Sanat&nbsp;Merkezi (Turkey), and Centro Público Integrado O Cruce (Spain).",
  "index.partnerOrgsTitle": "Partner Organizations in the Smart edu AI Project",
  "index.partner_eurolab_detail": "Eurolab for Teachers was founded five years ago by experienced teachers and trainers, with a mission to deliver high-quality professional development across Europe. Through the Erasmus+ program, a range of specialised courses blends modern teaching strategies, innovative tools, and intercultural perspectives—enhancing skills, fostering creativity, and promoting both personal and professional growth. Courses are offered in several European countries, designed to address the evolving needs of educators and encourage best practices that make a real difference in the classroom. The mission: shaping the future of education—one empowered teacher at a time.",
  "index.partner_duzce_detail": "This public, non-profit center educates gifted students aged 8 to 13 with a dedicated team of 8 teachers serving 112 students. It offers workshops across STEM fields, robotics, AI, music, painting, coding, and more, using a project-based, process-oriented learning model that encourages students to create tangible products. With experience in international programs such as Erasmus+ and eTwinning, the center is responsible for researching innovative AI educational practices, piloting AI applications, gathering student feedback, and making necessary adjustments. Additionally, it manages the project website and leads dissemination activities. The center spearheads the activity “Exploring the Art of Science with Artificial Intelligence.”",
  "index.partner_france_detail": "France Culture Connection is an NGO committed to social inclusion and skills development for people with disabilities and disadvantaged youth. The organization promotes digital and green transitions through a wide range of artistic, sports, environmental, and digital projects. It provides training in technology integration and digital tools such as Web 2.0, fablab, augmented and virtual reality initiation, coding (Html, CSS, Javascript, Python), digital citizenship, and cyberbullying awareness. France Culture Connection leads AI education training programs for teachers and educational staff, oversees quality control and impact assessment, designs the project’s digital logo, and supports educational content development. It leads the activity “Artificial Intelligence Training For Educators.”",
